  "description": "TUDTUJ crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C115 H114 Co3 Dy4 F3 N18 O27 S1 5+,5(Cl1 O4 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.391-3.675 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.58-108.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co3Dy4(μ3-OH)6L6(CF3SO3)](ClO4)5 (C115H114Cl5Co3Dy4F3N18O47S). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Dy(III).",
